<SddCritic keywords="critic, orchestrator, spec-review, task-review, blind-spot, multi-round, reconcile, surgical-edit, sdd-critic" type="directive" ver="2.1">
  <Mission>
    Autonomous critique loop for SDD artifacts (spec / task / batch). I am the ORCHESTRATOR: per round
    I dispatch one isolated critic-sensor, evaluate its findings against full project context, reconcile
    every introduced entity against the existing surface via `orient` (reuse > extend > justify >
    escalate), surgically edit the artifact, and re-dispatch if edits were applied (cap 5). Batch: the
    scope spec first, then tasks in DAG layers (parallel within a layer, sequential between). On CLEAN:
    delete the temporary `## Critic Rounds` scratch. I own the artifact and apply `MECHANICAL` edits; `GOAL`
    findings go to the operator as one batched question block first (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`). The sensor only reports.

    A separate door (`/sdd-critic`). Input — a spec / task / batch target. Output — the cleaned artifact
    + the final verdict.
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState>
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-language"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-dialogue-style"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-owner"}}

    {{> "axiom/boundary/ax-isolation-signal"}}

    {{> "axiom/truth/ax-reuse-first"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-surgical"}}

    {{> "axiom/critic/ax-default-accept"}}

    {{> "axiom/critic/ax-confusion-bug"}}

    {{> "axiom/critic/ax-finding-addressee"}}

    {{> "axiom/critic/ax-goal-owner-gate"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-rejection-reason"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-re-dispatch"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-stop-no-edits"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-cap-5"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-scratch-log"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-task-parallel"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_ARTIFACT` | The target spec / task does not exist |
    | `H_PARENT_SPEC_MISSING` | A task's parent spec is missing — cannot critique a task without its spec |
    | `H_DISPATCH_FAILED` | The sensor subagent failed to dispatch twice — surface to the operator, do not loop silently |
    | `H_MAX_ROUNDS` | Cap of 5 rounds hit and still not CLEAN — escalate to the operator (`AX_CAP_5`) |
    | `H_GOAL_BLOCKED` | `GOAL` findings block the round and the operator is unavailable to answer — stop, report the pending question block |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_RESOLVE">
      <Goal>Resolve the target.</Goal>
      <Action>Spec / task / batch (spec + its tasks — critiqued in DAG layers, parallel within a layer, per `AX_TASK_PARALLEL`). Missing → `H_NO_ARTIFACT`.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_DISPATCH">
      <Goal>Dispatch the isolated sensor.</Goal>
      <Action>One fresh subagent: read `ai/directives/sdd-v2/critic-protocol.directive.xml` + the artifact + parent spec only (`AX_ISOLATION_SIGNAL`). Emit a round progress line (`ORCHESTRATOR_PROGRESS_FORMAT`).</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_EVALUATE">
      <Goal>Weigh findings against full project context.</Goal>
      <Action>Split by addressee (`AX_FINDING_ADDRESSEE`): `MECHANICAL` — accept by default (`AX_DEFAULT_ACCEPT`); `GOAL` — queue for STEP_2C, keep the touched sections intact (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`). A rejection cites a specific file / section that resolves the concern (`AX_REJECTION_REASON`). Sensor confusion the full context resolves = an artifact bug — clarify by edit (`AX_CONFUSION_BUG`); confusion the project cannot answer = `GOAL`.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2B_RECONCILE">
      <Goal>Reconcile every introduced entity. (mechanical → tool)</Goal>
      <Action>For each entity a finding would add, run `orient` to check the existing project surface: reuse > extend > justify > escalate (`AX_REUSE_FIRST`). Do not let the critique invent a duplicate of an existing entity.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2C_GOAL_GATE">
      <Goal>Take `GOAL` findings to the goal owner (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`).</Goal>
      <Action>No `GOAL` findings → skip to STEP_3. Otherwise batch ALL of the round's `GOAL` findings into ONE question block (`QUESTION_FORMAT`, `Q<N>` with options; when the AskUserQuestion tool is available, ask through it) and WAIT — this precedes any edit to the sections they touch. Operator answers become edit instructions for STEP_3 and flow into the normal re-dispatch cycle. Operator unreachable while `GOAL` findings block → `H_GOAL_BLOCKED`.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_EDIT">
      <Goal>Apply surgical edits.</Goal>
      <Action>Edit only what a finding requires (`AX_SURGICAL`); I apply the edits — the sensor never does (`AX_OWNER`): `MECHANICAL` — directly; `GOAL` — exactly as the operator answered (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`). Record each in the temporary `## Critic Rounds` scratch (`AX_SCRATCH_LOG`).</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_DECIDE">
      <Goal>Loop or stop.</Goal>
      <Action>Edits applied → re-dispatch (`AX_RE_DISPATCH`). Zero edits → stop (`AX_STOP_NO_EDITS`). Cap 5 (`AX_CAP_5`) → `H_MAX_ROUNDS`.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_FINALIZE">
      <Goal>Finalize.</Goal>
      <Action>On CLEAN: delete the `## Critic Rounds` scratch; the artifact is clean with improvements integrated. Report the final verdict (CLEAN | NEEDS_WORK | CRITICAL) with a one-line-per-round summary of what changed. A structural problem the critique cannot resolve by a surgical edit → escalate to the operator, do not loop.</Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

  <ChatOutput>
    {{> "contract/process/question-format"}}

    {{> "contract/process/halt-format"}}

    {{> "contract/process/orchestrator-progress-format"}}
  </ChatOutput>
</SddCritic>
